# Telegram Volatility Alerts

This is an alert-only consumer of published data. Do not modify collector
ingest, parsing, spread calculation, storage lifecycle, `model.ipynb`,
private APIs or order routing from this scope.

Use only complete data available at the decision time:

- construct decisions on closed 5m windows;
- require 48-bar warmup, hysteresis, cooldown and explicit missing-data
  states;
- separate `manual_anomaly_label` from future `persistence_30m`;
- split offline evaluation by time and independent episode with embargo;
- prioritize event precision and false alerts per asset-day over accuracy.

ML is shadow-only until a locked holdout proves improvement over the
rule-only baseline. It must not silently change user delivery.

Telegram delivery requires a versioned idempotency key, append-only outbox,
observable `queued/sent/failed` accounting, retry-after handling and restart
recovery. Do not claim low latency before measuring closed-bar-to-send.
